        "question": {
          ":question/id": "739b0f57-a1b0-52bc-8be3-87f96d493abf",
          ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
          ":question/problem": "Calculate $$\n\\int x\\operatorname{cos}(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Write $I=\\int x\\operatorname{cos}(x)\\,\\text{d}x$. Use integration by parts.\n\n$$\n\\int uv^{\\prime}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=uv-\\int vu^{\\prime}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nChoose the linear factor as $u$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =x \\\\ u^{\\prime} & =1 \\\\ v^{\\prime} & =\\operatorname{cos}(x) \\\\ v & =\\operatorname{sin}(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute into the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}uv & =x\\left(\\operatorname{sin}(x)\\right) \\\\ \\int vu^{\\prime}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\left(\\operatorname{sin}(x)\\right)1\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate the remaining integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =x\\operatorname{sin}(x)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}(x)-(-\\operatorname{cos}(x))+C \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}(x)+\\operatorname{cos}(x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          ":question/answer-fields": [
