          ":question/problem": "Calculate $$\n\\int 3 x\\operatorname{csc}^{2}(x + 3)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Write $I=\\int 3 x\\operatorname{csc}^{2}(x + 3)\\,\\text{d}x$. Use integration by parts.\n\n$$\n\\int uv^{\\prime}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=uv-\\int vu^{\\prime}\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nChoose the linear factor as $u$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =3 x \\\\ u^{\\prime} & =3 \\\\ v^{\\prime} & =\\operatorname{csc}^{2}(x + 3) \\\\ v & =-\\operatorname{cot}(x + 3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute into the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}uv & =3 x\\left(-\\operatorname{cot}(x + 3)\\right) \\\\ \\int vu^{\\prime}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\left(-\\operatorname{cot}(x + 3)\\right)3\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse $t=\\operatorname{sin}(x + 3)$ and $\\mathrm{d}t=\\operatorname{cos}(x + 3)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$. Evaluate the remaining integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =-3 x\\operatorname{cot}(x + 3)+3\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}(x + 3)}{\\operatorname{sin}(x + 3)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3 x\\operatorname{cot}(x + 3)+3\\int \\frac{1}{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-3 x\\operatorname{cot}(x + 3)+3\\ln|t|+C \\\\  & =-3 x\\operatorname{cot}(x + 3)+3\\ln|\\operatorname{sin}(x + 3)|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis holds on each interval where $\\operatorname{sin}(x + 3)\\ne0$.",
